WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:05.300
A literature class reads classic Polish texts.

2
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.390
Litwo! Ojczyzno moja! ty jesteś jak zdrowie.

3
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:17.180
The opening of a famous epic poem from 1834, with two vocatives.

4
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.190
Nie przyszedł, albowiem był chory.

5
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.980
An elevated word for because.

6
00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.230
Chciał pomóc, lecz nie mógł.

7
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:30.820
A literary word for but.

8
00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:33.750
Ów człowiek zniknął bez śladu.

9
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.620
Panie, zmiłuj się nad nami.

10
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:43.420
The vocative case addresses someone directly.

11
00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:49.490
Older words replace their modern equivalents; recognising them is enough.

12
00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:56.930
He did not come, for he was ill. Use the elevated word.

13
00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:01.790
Nie przyszedł, albowiem był chory.

14
00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.350
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

15
00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:10.510
Nie przyszedł, albowiem był chory.

16
00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:16.110
That man vanished without a trace.

17
00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:20.890
Ów człowiek zniknął bez śladu.

18
00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:25.450
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

19
00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.530
Ów człowiek zniknął bez śladu.

20
00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:35.170
Now practise with the exercises below the video.
